# di API — DI (dependency injection) demo: computer <-> network
# Flow: POST /computer registers a computer in memory AND connects it to the
# network (via forwardRef circular DI); GET /network lists connected computers.

### 1. Run the computer — computes CPU + disk (note: no @Body needed)
GET http://localhost:3000/computer

### 2. Add a computer — stores it in memory + connects it to the network.
###    Returns 201 with an empty body (handler returns nothing).
POST http://localhost:3000/computer
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "ip": "127.0.0.3",
  "name": "Router"
}

### 3. Connected computers — lists computers registered via POST (network-side)
GET http://localhost:3000/network
